#: ui/pages.slint:4749
msgctxt "TransferPage"
msgid ""
"An encrypted backup is a copy of your vault file: it opens only with your "
"master password and Secret Key, or with your emergency kit. The copy is read "
"back and checked before the app calls it done. “Protected by a password” "
"is one file with every item, encrypted with a password you choose for it: "
"good for carrying your items to another computer, where Import reads it; it "
"has that one password only, so make it long. A KeePass database is encrypted "
"with a password (and a keyfile) you choose, for KeePass and the apps that "
"read its files. JSON, CSV and Credential Exchange are NOT encrypted: anyone "
"who gets the file can read every password (and, from a Credential Exchange "
"file, sign in with your passkeys), and malware looks for exactly these "
"files. Use them only to move to another password manager, then delete the "
"file."
msgstr ""

