#: ui/review.slint:57
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid ""
"This master password is easy to guess. Your Secret Key guards the vault too, "
"but anyone who also takes it from this computer (malware can) has only this "
"password left to find, and can try guesses for as long as they like. Six "
"random words are far harder to guess and still easy to type."
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:58
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid ""
"This password turned up in data breaches ({} times): attackers try those "
"first, on every site and file. Choose another one."
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:59
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid ""
"The breach check couldn't reach the service ({}). Nothing was sent except "
"the first five characters of the password's fingerprint."
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:60
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid ""
"This item password is easy to guess. Malware that copies the open vault from "
"memory could try guesses against it for as long as it likes, without this "
"app. Six random words are far harder to guess."
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:72
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid "Use a generated passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:76
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid "Go on without the check"
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:76
msgctxt "PasswordReview"
msgid "Keep this one"
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:89
msgctxt "LeakCheckBox"
msgid "Check it against known data breaches"
msgstr ""

#: ui/review.slint:95
msgctxt "LeakCheckBox"
msgid ""
"Before the password is used, the Have I Been Pwned service is asked whether "
"it appeared in a known breach. Only the first 5 characters of its SHA-1 "
"fingerprint leave this computer, never the password; the service answers "
"with hundreds of fingerprints that start the same way, and the match is made "
"here. Off until you tick it, since it uses the network."
msgstr ""

#: ui/strength.slint:45
msgctxt "StrengthMeter"
msgid "· {} bits"
msgstr ""

#: ui/strength.slint:53
msgctxt "StrengthMeter"
msgid ""
"Worst realistic case: a site you use is breached and its password list leaks "
"with fast (MD5) hashes. An attacker runs hashcat on six RTX 4090 graphics "
"cards, about a trillion guesses per second, and on average finds the "
"password halfway through. Sites that store passwords properly (bcrypt, "
"Argon2) make this millions of times slower. Each extra bit doubles the time."
msgstr ""

